   "title": "Photograph captions documenting the Kobe flood, views 7–67",
   "doc_type": "Photographic enclosure and caption list",
   "start_page": 81,
   "end_page": 102,
   "continues_previous": true,
   "date": "",
   "from": "",
   "to": "",
   "about": "Captions identify flood destruction throughout Kobe and rank the extent of damage in the city’s eight wards.",
   "summary": "The photographs show buried and destroyed houses, newly cut streambeds, damaged bridges and railway facilities, heavy silt deposits, and devastation around the Uji, Ōishi, and Sumiyoshi rivers. Numerous views document Kitanochō, Nada, Minato, Sannomiya, Motomachi, Nunobiki, and other parts of Kobe, including the damaged consulate and the home of Consul Walter P. McConaughy. The final page ranks Nada as the most severely affected ward, followed by Fukiai, Soto, Minato, Kobe, Suma, Hayashida, and Hyogo.",
   "keywords": [
